From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_IR_FREE=1: a boot pipeline build frees its shader IR before its driver compile (Lichii #878); EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_RUNTIME=1 also after a translation during play; EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_LOG=1 logs the sizes only; all off by default

Port of zortos293/Lichii #878 ("vulkan: free compute IR before a synchronous driver compile", merged
as fd4ce24c9b; commits 7bb2fc70e8 and 809b63b683). Our out-of-memory crashes die in RADV NIR's
ralloc during a pipeline compile (nir_opt_copy_prop_vars.c:419, VkPipelineBuilder, 9 and 10 Nov). A
build kept its translated IR (the inst and block pools, the program's block lists, and for compute
the SPIR-V words) until it returned. The boot's disk cache (LoadDiskResources) and the shader
preparation and its probes (PrepareKept) build with no thread worker, so the driver compile runs
inside the pipeline's constructor and every builder held its IR through its compile. Lichii
measured ~323 MiB of pool memory for one large Ocarina compute program and ~1077 MiB held across 24
workers at its compute precache peak; with the PR, 35-41 MiB and an ~850 MiB lower peak commit,
with no change in the phase's time.

EDEN_UP_IR_FREE=1 acts at boot only. Every build whose compile runs on the calling thread is in
LoadDiskResources or PrepareKept; during play nothing changes, so this switch alone does not reach
the door crashes. (With the shader-set series stacked and EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET=1, PrepareShaderSet's
background jobs build the same way and free too, and those may run during play.) Up to 15 builders
compile at once at boot (hardware threads minus one, unless EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_WORKERS caps it).
Scaling Lichii's 1077 MiB to 15 builders gives roughly 650-700 MiB off the boot peak (about 180-190
MiB at 4 builders). Unmeasured on PS5.

With the switch, a build whose compile runs on the calling thread (graphics and compute) drops the
programs' block lists, frees the block pool and then the instruction pool (blocks first: a block's
instruction list unlinks its instructions as it goes) and, for compute, the SPIR-V words, right
before the pipeline is constructed. Unlike Lichii, the programs' infos stay in place: the pipelines
copy them (ComputePipeline's info{info_}, GraphicsPipeline's stage_infos) before the compile, which
reads only the shader modules (the driver holds their SPIR-V) and those copies. Shader::Info holds
no pointers into the IR. The flow-block pool stays: the compute CFG lives until the build returns,
and the graphics error path walks a CFG with it. ObjectPool::Free() allocates nothing: the pool
makes its next chunk at its next Create. So a free when memory is short cannot leave the pool
pointing at a chunk it gave back (a failed new chunk would have, with SurviveBadAlloc letting the
session go on), and a boot builder makes no new chunk right before its compile.

Where the freed memory goes: an instruction chunk (8192 instructions, about 1 MiB) is over the
heap's 256 KiB small-request line, so it lives in the heap's shared spaces, not in the builder's
own arenas. Only a block of 32 MiB or more has memory of its own, and that goes back to the system
when freed. RADV's small requests go to the thread's arenas first, so the freed room helps the
compile only when they spill into the shared spaces, when a new 2 MiB arena fits in a freed hole,
or when a trim gives back a 32 MiB piece that emptied.

EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_RUNTIME=1 does the same for a build whose compile is queued on a builder: a
pipeline translated during play in main_pools on the GPU thread. Lichii left this path alone to
keep the pools' room for the next translation. Here ReleaseContents squashes a filled pool into one
block of the largest translation so far, and PS5 direct memory is committed from its first byte, so
main_pools holds that much for the session. With the switch it goes back after each build (to the
system if 32 MiB or more, else to the shared spaces), and the next translation allocates its ~1 MiB
chunks again. This is the only switch that acts at doors, and it saves one pool's room above the
current translation, not that of many builders: likely tens of MiB. Graphics pipelines made during
play from the shader-prep store skip translation, so there it helps only through compute builds and
pipelines the store does not hold. Its cost is to be measured: each translation during play
allocates its chunks again under the heap's shared lock, and the GPU thread does not wait for
memory (EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_MS covers builders only). Under pressure, a translation that used to
reuse held room can be refused, its pipeline dropped and its draws skipped. Compare the "built on
the GPU thread in N ms" and "No memory for" lines of a door run with the switch on and off.

EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_LOG=1 frees nothing and logs sizes, for sizing before a door slot is spent on
_RUNTIME: every build translated on the GPU thread (first 2000) logs its pools' size, which is
main_pools' size, with the hash of its "built on the GPU thread" line. A builder's job whose pools
hold 32 MiB or more logs too (first 100).

Log line: "EDEN_UP_IR_FREE: <kind> <hash> (builder|GPU thread): U MiB of IR in use, H MiB held,
freed|kept before its driver compile". With a free switch, a build whose pools held 32 MiB or more logs it
(first 100); the gate is the held size, so main_pools' one release of its large block shows even
when the build that releases it used little of it. A log line that finds no memory is skipped and
the build goes on.

The three names are not in TranslationSwitches (vk_pipeline_prep.cpp) on purpose: they change no
SPIR-V or info, so test arms share one prep store. EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_KEEP is left out the same
way.

Unset, or anything but "1": nothing is freed early and no line is logged. The edits on that path:
the compute SPIR-V vector loses its const, ObjectPool::FreeChunk checks node for null first (it is
never null without Free), and three cached switch reads. Not ported: Lichii's ObjectPool::Free unit
tests.

---
 src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h                  | 30 ++++++++++++++-
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp | 81 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h b/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h
index c39d352..841c273 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h
@@ -23,6 +23,33 @@ public:
         return std::construct_at(Memory(), std::forward<Args>(args)...);
     }
 
+    /// Destroys the objects and returns their memory; ReleaseContents keeps it for reuse.
+    /// Allocates nothing: the next Create makes a fresh chunk, so a pool freed when memory is
+    /// short is never left pointing at a chunk it gave back.
+    void Free() noexcept {
+        node = nullptr;
+        chunks.clear();
+        chunks.shrink_to_fit();
+    }
+
+    /// Bytes of the objects made since the last release or free
+    [[nodiscard]] size_t UsedBytes() const noexcept {
+        size_t used{};
+        for (const Chunk& chunk : chunks) {
+            used += chunk.used_objects;
+        }
+        return used * sizeof(Storage);
+    }
+
+    /// Bytes the pool has allocated, used or not
+    [[nodiscard]] size_t HeldBytes() const noexcept {
+        size_t held{};
+        for (const Chunk& chunk : chunks) {
+            held += chunk.num_objects;
+        }
+        return held * sizeof(Storage);
+    }
+
     void ReleaseContents() {
         if (chunks.empty()) {
             return;
@@ -96,7 +123,8 @@ private:
     }
 
     [[nodiscard]] Chunk* FreeChunk() {
-        if (node->used_objects != node->num_objects) {
+        // Null only after Free(), and only until a chunk is made: if that throws, still null.
+        if (node != nullptr && node->used_objects != node->num_objects) {
             return node;
         }
         node = &chunks.emplace_back(new_chunk_size);
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 5f97bb0..081f571 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -434,6 +434,70 @@ size_t GetTotalPipelineWorkers() {
 #endif
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_IR_FREE=1 (exact "1", Lichii #878): a build whose driver compile runs on the calling
+// thread frees its translated IR before that compile instead of when the build returns. Those
+// are a builder's jobs with their own pools: here only at boot (LoadDiskResources' disk cache,
+// PrepareKept's shader preparation and its probes), so a pipeline made during play is as
+// before. Up to 15 builders compile at once there, and each held its IR (up to hundreds of MiB
+// for one large program) beside the driver's own compile memory.
+// EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_RUNTIME=1: a build whose compile is queued on a builder (a pipeline made
+// during play, translated in main_pools on the GPU thread) frees it too, instead of main_pools
+// keeping the room of its largest translation so far; the next translation allocates again.
+// EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_LOG=1: sizing only, nothing freed. Every build translated on the GPU thread
+// logs its pools' size (main_pools at a door), and so does a builder's job holding 32 MiB+.
+// Unset, or anything but "1": all as before.
+enum class IrFree { Keep, Log, Free };
+[[nodiscard]] IrFree IrFreeMode(bool compiled_later) {
+    static const bool before_compile = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_IR_FREE");
+    static const bool runtime = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_RUNTIME");
+    static const bool log_only = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_IR_FREE_LOG");
+    if (compiled_later ? runtime : before_compile) {
+        return IrFree::Free;
+    }
+    return log_only ? IrFree::Log : IrFree::Keep;
+}
+
+// Reads the pools' size, then (IrFree::Free) drops the translated programs' IR: their block
+// lists, which point into the pools, then the pools' blocks and instructions, blocks first (a
+// block's instruction list unlinks its instructions as it goes). The programs' infos stay, for
+// the pipeline to copy. The flow blocks stay too: a live CFG may still hold them, and they are
+// small. Nothing here allocates but the log line, and a log line that finds no memory is skipped.
+void FreeIr(ShaderPools& pools, std::span<Shader::IR::Program> programs, IrFree mode,
+            bool compiled_later, const char* kind, u64 hash) {
+    const size_t used{pools.inst.UsedBytes() + pools.block.UsedBytes()};
+    const size_t held{pools.inst.HeldBytes() + pools.block.HeldBytes()};
+    const bool frees{mode == IrFree::Free};
+    if (frees) {
+        for (Shader::IR::Program& program : programs) {
+            program.syntax_list = Shader::IR::AbstractSyntaxList{};
+            program.blocks = Shader::IR::BlockList{};
+            program.post_order_blocks = Shader::IR::BlockList{};
+        }
+        pools.block.Free();
+        pools.inst.Free();
+    }
+    // Gated on the held size, so the one release of main_pools' large block shows even when the
+    // build that releases it used little of it (first 100). Sizing only: every build translated on
+    // the GPU thread (first 2000), to compare with its "built on the GPU thread" line by hash.
+    static std::atomic<u32> large_lines{};
+    static std::atomic<u32> sizing_lines{};
+    const bool logs{(!frees && compiled_later)
+                        ? sizing_lines.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) < 2000
+                        : held >= (size_t{32} << 20) &&
+                              large_lines.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) < 100};
+    if (!logs) {
+        return;
+    }
+    try {
+        LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                 "EDEN_UP_IR_FREE: {} {:016x} ({}): {:.1f} MiB of IR in use, {:.1f} MiB held, {} "
+                 "before its driver compile",
+                 kind, hash, compiled_later ? "GPU thread" : "builder", used / 1048576.0,
+                 held / 1048576.0, frees ? "freed" : "kept");
+    } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+    }
+}
+
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 size_t ComputePipelineCacheKey::Hash() const noexcept {
@@ -2204,6 +2268,12 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline(
                                         ? prep_no_cache
                                         : vulkan_pipeline_cache};
     Common::ThreadWorker* const thread_worker{build_in_parallel ? &workers : nullptr};
+    if (const IrFree ir_free{IrFreeMode(thread_worker != nullptr)}; ir_free != IrFree::Keep) {
+        // From here on the pipeline reads the modules (the driver holds their SPIR-V),
+        // mesh_compute (its own copies) and the infos, which stay in programs and are copied
+        // before the compile. kept_out holds copies too.
+        FreeIr(pools, programs, ir_free, thread_worker != nullptr, "graphics pipeline", hash);
+    }
     return std::make_unique<GraphicsPipeline>(
         scheduler, buffer_cache, texture_cache, driver_cache, &shader_notify, device,
         descriptor_pool, guest_descriptor_queue, descriptor_buffer_ring, thread_worker, statistics,
@@ -2445,7 +2515,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<ComputePipeline> PipelineCache::CreateComputePipeline(
                     max_shared_memory / 1024);
         program.shared_memory_size = max_shared_memory;
     }
-    const std::vector<u32> code{EmitSPIRV(profile, program)};
+    std::vector<u32> code{EmitSPIRV(profile, program)};
     device.SaveShader(code);
     vk::ShaderModule spv_module{BuildShader(device, code)};
 
@@ -2474,6 +2544,15 @@ std::unique_ptr<ComputePipeline> PipelineCache::CreateComputePipeline(
         compute_null_slots[key].slots = env.NullStoragePointerSlots();
     }
     Common::ThreadWorker* const thread_worker{build_in_parallel ? &workers : nullptr};
+    if (const IrFree ir_free{IrFreeMode(thread_worker != nullptr)}; ir_free != IrFree::Keep) {
+        // From here on the pipeline reads program.info, which stays and is copied first, and
+        // spv_module, whose SPIR-V the driver holds: the words and the IR are not read again.
+        FreeIr(pools, std::span{&program, 1}, ir_free, thread_worker != nullptr,
+               "compute shader", key.unique_hash);
+        if (ir_free == IrFree::Free) {
+            code = std::vector<u32>{};
+        }
+    }
     return std::make_unique<ComputePipeline>(device, scheduler, vulkan_pipeline_cache, descriptor_pool,
                                              guest_descriptor_queue, descriptor_buffer_ring,
                                              thread_worker, statistics,
